    "knowledge_point": "Determining the Equation of a Parabola Passing Through a Given Point",
    "problem": "Find the equation of the upward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and which passes through the point $(-5,5).$",
    "worked_solution": "We know that for any upward or downward-opening parabola whose vertex is $(0,0),$ the general standard equation is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant.\n\nWe're told that the given parabola passes through the point $(-5,5),$ so we can substitute $x=-5$ and $y=5$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4py \\\\ (-5)^{2} & =4p(5) \\\\ 25 & =20p \\\\ p & =\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4py \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4(\\frac{5}{4})y \\\\ {x}^{2} & =5y.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
