    "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. For a vertical parabola, write (x-h)^2=c(y-k), where c=(x_0-h)^2/(y_0-k). Using each vertex and supplied point gives: q-11779 c=-4/3; q-11781 c=8/3; q-115432 c=4; q-11792 c=5; q-115451 c=2; q-115502 c=-12; q-115513 c=-9/4; and q-11833 c=-7. For q-122888, x'=8sin(4t), y'=24cos(4t), and dy/dx=3cot(4t); differentiating with respect to t and dividing by x' gives -(3/2)csc^3(4t), wherever sin(4t) is nonzero. For q-80136, coefficient matching gives tan(phi)=8/2=4, so phi=arctan(4), interpreted in degrees as requested. For q-107570 and q-80138, equal positive sine and negative cosine coefficients give phase 45 degrees and amplitudes sqrt(10) and 4sqrt(2), respectively. For q-107579, tan(phi)=(2sqrt(2))/(2sqrt(6))=1/sqrt(3), so phi=pi/6. For q-51145, clearing denominators gives coefficients B-2=-3 and 4-B=5, both yielding B=-1. For q-49723, coefficient matching gives A+C=0, B-2A=7, and -2B+3C=0; hence A=-2, B=3, C=2 and their sum is 3. For q-102561, matching coefficients gives A+C=3, 5A+B=2, and 5B+6C=-3, yielding A=1, B=-3, C=2. No submitted grades or earlier answers are supplied; confirmation rests on the captured worked solutions and independent mathematical verification.",
